<title>USA: Brent crude slips in late U.S. paper trading.</title>
<headline>Brent crude slips in late U.S. paper trading.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Sea Benchmark Brent crude slipped in late U.S. paper trading on Tuesday, traders said.</p>
<p>Eight partial July cargoes traded 100 times apiece between $18.10 and $18.14 a barrel.</p>
<p>The July contract on London's IPE settled at $18.13 a barrel.</p>
<p>June/July Brent traded twice at minus 16 cents, down a penny from an earlier trade.</p>
<p>May/June was talked at minus 20-15 cents, while July/August was talked at minus 14-13 cents.</p>
<p>--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
